.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH REPOSYNC 8
.SH NAME
reposync \- synchronize git repositories (Qwaderton Linux repo sync)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBreposync\fR keeps local git checkouts of the distribution repositories
(recipe repos, build scripts, documentation) up to date. Repositories
are defined entirely by environment variables, so the tool has no
configuration file of its own and is safe to run from cron or boot
scripts.
.LP
For each repository: if the target directory is not a git checkout, it
is cloned (shallow, single branch); otherwise the checkout is fetched,
hard-reset to the upstream branch, and cleaned of untracked files. When
the HEAD changes, a diffstat of the update is printed.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR
Dry run. Print the commands that would run without executing them.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR
Log output to \fI/var/log/reposync.log\fR in addition to stdout.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR
Force: remove existing checkouts before syncing.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Print usage and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.LP
Each repository is defined by a variable named \fIREPOSYNC_<name>\fR
with the value \fIurl|branch|path\fR:
.RS
.nf

REPOSYNC_core="https://codeberg.org/qwaderton/core.git|master|/var/repo/core"

.fi
.RE
.LP
All \fIREPOSYNC_*\fR variables found in the environment are processed in
sorted order.

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/var/log/reposync.log\fR
Log file used with \fB\-l\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amu (8),
.BR git (1)

